WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.680
Readers, beware. The fifth episode&nbsp;
of "House of the Dragon" changes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.220
key detail from "Fire and Blood,"&nbsp;
and one character looks all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:12.300
more sinister for it. Spoilers for&nbsp;
both the book and the show ahead.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.280
Divisive final season aside, it's pretty&nbsp;
obvious that Game of Thrones has become a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.360
permanent staple in pop culture. Now, it&nbsp;
seems, every detail about the characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:26.220
confrontations, and locations in author&nbsp;
George R. R. Martin's world has become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:31.080
ingrained in viewers' brains. From the names of&nbsp;
the Targaryens' dragons to the banners of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.030
houses of Westeros, Martin's world won't soon&nbsp;
be forgotten by fans of the classic series .

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:40.920
Thankfully, these morsels of TV-related trivia&nbsp;
have become an enormous help with our return trip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.780
to the Seven Kingdoms in House of the Dragon.&nbsp;
Fans might struggle after being thrown into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:50.580
world so far removed from the events of Game&nbsp;
of Thrones, but the world itself is thankfully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:54.420
familiar enough to give them the lay of the&nbsp;
land. In the case of this week's episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:59.520
though, one notable landmark made an appearance&nbsp;
— one that has a well-known history of its own.&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:05.160
House of the Dragon's fifth episode, "We Light&nbsp;
The Way," features the short-lived debut of Rhea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:10.560
Royce , the estranged wife of Daemon Targaryen.&nbsp;
The unhappy couple is reunited under the king's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.700
orders after King Viserys commands his&nbsp;
brother to return to the Eyrie following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:19.200
a recent scandal. And the location of their&nbsp;
reunion that holds particular significance.&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.400
Those that are only familiar with the TV&nbsp;
adaptation of Game of Thrones will remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:28.560
that the first time the Vale appeared in the show&nbsp;
was when Catelyn Stark visited her sister Lysa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.720
Tully in the show's first season. It's also where&nbsp;
the friendship of Bronn and Tyrion began after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:38.700
former fought in a trial by combat.
"You don't fight with honor."&nbsp;

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.620
"He did."
The location was notorious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.960
for its impregnable castle, known as the Eyrie.&nbsp;
Marked by steep paths and high vantage points,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.100
the fortress has a solid track record&nbsp;
of maintaining the home turf against the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:58.080
enemy — that is, until Daemon wandered through&nbsp;
the land with nothing but a rock and an attitude.&nbsp;

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:03.300
Yes, in House of the Dragon, Daemon Targaryen&nbsp;
basically manages to infiltrate and kill the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.740
Vale's only defender: his wife, Rhea&nbsp;
Royce. It's an impressive victory for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.060
Daemon — and more than a little grisly — but&nbsp;
this scene also features a significant change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.440
from George R. R. Martin's original work.
In Fire and Blood, the book from which the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:21.540
show is adapted, Rhea meets a similar end, but&nbsp;
it's one that takes much longer. While she does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:25.560
fall from her horse and crack her head on a&nbsp;
rock, she then lives for another nine days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:30.660
bedridden. When she eventually does get up, she&nbsp;
collapses an hour later, and finally succumbs to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:35.100
her injuries. Notably, Daemon doesn't kill Rhea&nbsp;
in the book. In fact, he's off fighting a war,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.180
many miles away, when it happens. 
 
However, the show's version of events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:44.100
adds another layer of deception and cunning to&nbsp;
Daemon's character. Here, Rhea is just another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.780
piece to move to how he sees fit. By the end&nbsp;
of the episode, Daemon is already at work not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:54.300
only in brushing off accusations regarding Rhea's&nbsp;
death, but also in making moves on Laena Velaryon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:58.440
daughter of Corlys. He's certainly&nbsp;
not killing time, that's for sure.

